BaFi Convert JSON, XML, CSV, YAML, BSON and MT940 into any text format with templates. bafi reads structured data from a file or a pipe and renders it through a template into whatever text the next system needs: JSON, XML, CSV, HTML, SQL, a SOAP request. One small program without dependencies for Windows, macOS and Linux. Install · Recipes · Function reference · Troubleshooting · GitHub What do you want to do? I want to... Recipe turn XML into JSON Convert XML to JSON turn JSON (e.g. a REST response) into XML Convert JSON to XML turn a CSV export into JSON Convert CSV to JSON get JSON or XML into Excel Convert JSON to CSV · XML to CSV call a SOAP service with data from a REST API REST response to SOAP request give a SOAP response to a REST client SOAP response to JSON produce an HTML report HTML report from JSON load a CSV into a database SQL INSERT statements from CSV process MT940 bank statements MT940 to CSV combine several files into one document Merge several files convert YAML, JSON, TOON, BSON Convert between formats All recipes In thirty seconds {"users": [{"name": "Alice", "city": "Prague"}, {"name": "Bob", "city": "Brno"}]} Convert the whole document with one function: bafi -i users.json -t '?{{toYAML .}}' users: - city: Prague name: Alice - city: Brno name: Bob Or describe the output yourself. Text outside {{ }} is copied as it is; range repeats a block for every item: bafi -i users.json -t '?{{range .users}}{{.name}} lives in {{upper .city}}{{"
"}}{{end}}' Alice lives in PRAGUE Bob lives in BRNO Works in pipes too: curl -fs https://example.com/api/users | bafi -f json -t report.tmpl -o report.html . Next: the template guide and the command line . Try it online Runs entirely in your browser; nothing is uploaded. The demo (a few megabytes) loads on the first click. JSON to text CSV to JSON XML to CSV Input format: JSON XML YAML CSV Run var bafiExamples = { json: {format: "json", input: '{
 "user": {
 "name": "John Doe",
 "age": 25,
 "address": {"city": "New York", "state": "NY"},
 "favourite_colors": ["red", "green", "blue"]
 }
}', template: 'Hello {{upper .user.name}},

you are {{.user.age}} years old
and live in {{.user.address.city}}, {{.user.address.state}}.
Your favourite colors are:
{{range .user.favourite_colors}} - {{.}}
{{end}}'}, csv: {format: "csv", input: 'id,name,city
1,Alice,Prague
2,"Brown, Bob",Brno', template: '{{toJSON .}}'}, xml: {format: "xml", input: '<orders>
 <order id="1001"><customer>Alice</customer><total>120.50</total></order>
 <order id="1002"><customer>Bob</customer><total>80.00</total></order>
</orders>', template: 'id,customer,total
{{- range mustArray .orders.order}}
{{index . "-id"}},{{.customer}},{{.total}}
{{- end}}'} }; function bafiExample(name) { var e = bafiExamples[name]; document.getElementById("bafiFormat").value = e.format; document.getElementById("bafiInput").value = e.input; document.getElementById("bafiTemplate").value = e.template; document.getElementById("bafiOutput").textContent = ""; } var bafiLoading = null; function bafiLoad() { if (!bafiLoading) { var go = new Go(); bafiLoading = WebAssembly.instantiateStreaming(fetch("js/bafi.wasm"), go.importObject) .then(function (result) { go.run(result.instance); }); } return bafiLoading; } function bafiRun() { var out = document.getElementById("bafiOutput"); if (typeof bafiRender !== "function") { out.textContent = "Loading the demo..."; } bafiLoad().then(function () { out.textContent = bafiRender(document.getElementById("bafiInput").value, document.getElementById("bafiTemplate").value, document.getElementById("bafiFormat").value); }).catch(function (err) { bafiLoading = null; out.textContent = "The demo could not be loaded: " + err; }); } bafiExample("json"); Why bafi Many inputs: JSON, BSON, YAML, CSV (any delimiter), XML and MT940 bank statements, from a file or standard input. Any output: the template decides. HTML, SQL, shell scripts, SOAP envelopes, fixed-width text. Pipes: read from curl , write to the next command. Bridges REST and SOAP services, databases and spreadsheets. Several inputs at once: merge files of different formats into one output. Helpful errors: problems are reported with the file, line and column, and a hint how to fix them. Extensible: 60+ template functions, plus your own in Lua . TOON and OpenAI: encode data compactly for LLM prompts, or ask OpenAI about your data (experimental). If you like this app you can buy me a coffee ;)

